course: dictionary
lesson: 6102
title: Milligrams and mg
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: mg is short for milligram, a very small unit of mass. A milligram is a tiny amount, so you need many of them to make a gram. «In the UK, drinks with more than 150 mg of caffeine per litre must carry the warning «High caffeine content.»» Here 150 mg is a small amount of caffeine, weighed in milligrams.
explain: Sizes help you compare. There are 1,000 mg in 1 gram, and 1,000,000 mg in 1 kilogram. So when you convert g to mg, multiply by 1,000. Check your answer: a milligram should be a much smaller number than the gram it came from.
explain: On food and medicine labels, mg tells you how much of a vitamin, salt or medicine is in one dose. «A small 250 ml can at 32 mg per 100 ml holds about 80 mg of caffeine, and a 500 ml can about 160 mg, roughly like two cups of instant coffee.» Read the label to find the amount, then keep to it.
fact: mg is short for milligram, a unit of mass.
fact: 1 gram = 1,000 mg, and 1 kilogram = 1,000,000 mg.
fact: To convert grams to milligrams, multiply by 1,000.
fact: «500 mg tablet» means the tablet has 500 milligrams of medicine in it.
fact: Only adults should give medicine, and never take more than the label says.
fact: MG (in capitals) is also a British car brand, so check the context: a number before mg means an amount, and MG before a car means the brand.
exercise: How many milligrams are in 1 gram? | 10 | 100 | 1,000,000 | *1,000
exercise: «A small 250 ml can at 32 mg per 100 ml holds about 80 mg of caffeine, and a 500 ml can about 160 mg.» How much caffeine is in the 500 ml can? | 250 mg | 32 mg | 80 mg | *160 mg
exercise: Which amount is the biggest? | 500 mg | 900 mg | *1 g | 1 mg
test: Convert 2 g to mg. | 200 mg | 2,000,000 mg | 20 mg | *2,000 mg
test: On a medicine label, what does mg tell you? | *How much medicine is in one dose | The name of the shop that sold it | The date it expires | The time to take it
exam: A child finds a «500 mg tablet» at home and wants to take it. What should they do? | Swallow it with a glass of juice | *Tell an adult and leave it alone | Take two to be safe | Give it to a friend who has a headache
